## How this portfolio is organized
Each project above lives in its own folder here for review, and is meant to become its own standalone GitHub repository (see `GIT_SETUP.md` in this same package for the exact commands). Numbering reflects the order the material was actually covered, from Python fundamentals through model optimization and medical imaging.

## A note on chart rendering
GitHub renders a Jupyter notebook's saved cell outputs directly, including matplotlib/seaborn charts, as long as the notebook was **run before being committed** (outputs embedded in the `.ipynb` JSON). All 18 notebooks above now have their outputs saved and are ready to push as-is.
